Advanced API Operations
Subtask 5.1: Bulk Operations with API
Create multiple job templates using a loop:
cat > create_multiple_templates.sh << 'EOF'
#!/bin/bash

AWX_TOKEN=$1
AWX_HOST=$2
PROJECT_ID=$3
INVENTORY_ID=$4

for i in {1..3}; do
    cat > bulk_template_$i.json << EOF
{
  "name": "Bulk-Template-$i",
  "description": "Bulk created template $i",
  "job_type": "run",
  "inventory": $INVENTORY_ID,
  "project": $PROJECT_ID,
  "playbook": "lamp_simple/site.yml",
  "verbosity": 1
}
EOF

    echo "Creating template $i..."
    curl -X POST \
         -H "Authorization: Bearer $AWX_TOKEN" \
         -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
         -d @bulk_template_$i.json \
         "$AWX_HOST/api/v2/job_templates/"
    
    echo "Template $i created"
    sleep 1
done
EOF

chmod +x create_multiple_templates.sh
Run the bulk creation script:
./create_multiple_templates.sh $AWX_TOKEN $AWX_HOST $PROJECT_ID $INVENTORY_ID
Subtask 5.2: API Error Handling
Create a script with proper error handling:
cat > api_with_error_handling.sh << 'EOF'
#!/bin/bash

AWX_TOKEN=$1
AWX_HOST=$2

make_api_call() {
    local method=$1
    local endpoint=$2
    local data=$3
    
    if [ -n "$data" ]; then
        response=$(curl -s -w "\n%{http_code}" -X "$method" \
                       -H "Authorization: Bearer $AWX_TOKEN" \
                       -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
                       -d "$data" \
                       "$AWX_HOST$endpoint")
    else
        response=$(curl -s -w "\n%{http_code}" -X "$method" \
                       -H "Authorization: Bearer $AWX_TOKEN" \
                       -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
                       "$AWX_HOST$endpoint")
    fi
    
    http_code=$(echo "$response" | tail -n1)
    body=$(echo "$response" | head -n -1)
    
    if [[ $http_code -ge 200 && $http_code -lt 300 ]]; then
        echo "Success: $http_code"
        echo "$body" | jq '.' 2>/dev/null || echo "$body"
        return 0
    else
        echo "Error: HTTP $http_code"
        echo "$body" | jq '.' 2>/dev/null || echo "$body"
        return 1
    fi
}

# Test with a valid endpoint
echo "Testing valid endpoint:"
make_api_call "GET" "/api/v2/ping/"

echo
echo "Testing invalid endpoint:"
make_api_call "GET" "/api/v2/nonexistent/"
EOF

chmod +x api_with_error_handling.sh
Run the error handling demonstration:
./api_with_error_handling.sh $AWX_TOKEN $AWX_HOST
Troubleshooting Common Issues
Authentication Issues
Token Expired: If you receive 401 errors, your token may have expired. Create a new token:
# Check token validity
curl -H "Authorization: Bearer $AWX_TOKEN" \
     -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
     "$AWX_HOST/api/v2/me/"
Insufficient Permissions: Ensure your user has the necessary permissions:
# Check user permissions
curl -H "Authorization: Bearer $AWX_TOKEN" \
     -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
     "$AWX_HOST/api/v2/me/" | jq '.results[0].summary_fields.user_capabilities'
Project Sync Issues
Project Not Syncing: Check project status and errors:
curl -H "Authorization: Bearer $AWX_TOKEN" \
     -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
     "$AWX_HOST/api/v2/projects/$PROJECT_ID/" | jq '{status: .status, scm_revision: .scm_revision, last_job: .summary_fields.last_job}'
Job Execution Issues
Job Stuck in Pending: Check system capacity and running jobs:
# Check system capacity
curl -H "Authorization: Bearer $AWX_TOKEN" \
     -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
     "$AWX_HOST/api/v2/settings/system/" | jq '.SYSTEM_TASK_ABS_CPU'

# Check running jobs
curl -H "Authorization: Bearer $AWX_TOKEN" \
     -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
     "$AWX_HOST/api/v2/jobs/?status=running"
Cleanup
Remove created resources:
# Delete job templates
for template in "Lab17-Demo-Job-Template" "Bulk-Template-1" "Bulk-Template-2" "Bulk-Template-3"; do
    TEMPLATE_ID=$(curl -s -H "Authorization: Bearer $AWX_TOKEN" \
                       -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
                       "$AWX_HOST/api/v2/job_templates/?name=$template" | \
                       jq -r '.results[0].id')
    
    if [ "$TEMPLATE_ID" != "null" ]; then
        curl -X DELETE \
             -H "Authorization: Bearer $AWX_TOKEN" \
             "$AWX_HOST/api/v2/job_templates/$TEMPLATE_ID/"
        echo "Deleted template: $template"
    fi
done

# Delete inventory
curl -X DELETE \
     -H "Authorization: Bearer $AWX_TOKEN" \
     "$AWX_HOST/api/v2/inventories/$INVENTORY_ID/"

# Delete project
curl -X DELETE \
     -H "Authorization: Bearer $AWX_TOKEN" \
     "$AWX_HOST/api/v2/projects/$PROJECT_ID/"
